Resident Commit and Abort Case
===============================================================================

The Rust veneer loads the program below through the new v0.4 resident route.
It then uses the same runtime's explicit transaction shell to treat the first
mailbox message as the initial state and the second as the committed state.
Popping the first message is staged, so the second is transaction-visible; an
abort restores the first, while a commit makes the second durable.

-- @case-id resident-transaction-commit-and-abort
-- @requirements RES-001 RES-002 TURN-001 TURN-002 TURN-003 TURN-004 TURN-005 LIFE-001
-- @initial-state state-before
-- @committed-state state-after

-- @resident-program
~conformance-state := "state-after"
next-turn-state := conformance-state
